---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Contact — World Cup Draft Simulator"
  description="Contact World Cup Draft Simulator with feedback, bug reports and questions about the fantasy football World Cup draft simulation game."
>

<main class="min-h-screen bg-canvas text-white">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 text-center">
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase">
      Contact
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl leading-[0.9] tracking-[1.07px] sm:text-6xl">
      Get in touch
    </h1>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-xl text-secondary">
      Feedback, bug reports, feature ideas or questions about World Cup Draft
      Simulator — the free online soccer game and browser soccer game where you
      draft and simulate your own World Cup? We'd love to hear from you. This is
      a fantasy football world cup project built by fans of the tournament, so
      every message shapes what the soccer simulator becomes next. Whether you
      found us as a soccer draft game, a free soccer simulation game or an
      interactive soccer simulator, the door is open: tell us a squad that feels
      mis-rated, a match that swung too hard, or a feature the football draft
      simulator should add. There is no account to manage and no download to
      reinstall, so reaching out is as quick as playing a round.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <a
        href="mailto:contact@example.com?subject=World%20Cup%20Draft%20Simulator%20Feedback"
        class="inline-block rounded-full bg-mint px-8 py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-black uppercase transition-colors duration-150 hover:bg-white"
      >
        Email us
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto mt-12 max-w-md border-t border-white/10 pt-8 text-left">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-[1.5px] text-secondary uppercase">
        Email
      </p>
        <p class="mt-1">
          <a class="text-mint underline" href="mailto:contact@example.com">contact@example.com</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mx-auto mt-12 max-w-md border-t border-white/10 pt-8 text-left text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
        <p>
          When you write in, a few details help us act fast. If a match in the
          world cup simulation felt off, mention the formations involved and the
          round — group stage or knockout bracket — so we can see how the match
          engine resolved it. If a player rating looks wrong, name the squad and
          the position, because the football simulator compares every draft on
          one scale and a single outlier can tilt a tournament. Feature ideas
          are just as welcome: more historical squads, extra football formations,
          a deeper penalty shootout simulator, or a way to share your finished
          cup are all on the table for a world cup fantasy game that keeps
          growing. We also love hearing from communities that run a fantasy soccer
          draft or coach a youth side and want a free browser soccer game for
          the classroom or the locker room — the online soccer game runs on any
          device with no sign-up, which makes it easy to drop into a lesson or a
          match-day warm-up. Because this is a soccer game no download, you can
          open it, play a round, and tell us what you would change in the same
          sitting. However you found us — as a world cup simulator, a soccer
          draft game, or simply the easiest interactive soccer simulator to open
          between matches — your notes make the next build better, so get in
          touch and help shape the app you play.
        </p>
      </div>
  </section>
</main></Layout>
